===== Did selection transfer? =====
Rank correlation between what the search maximized (train fitness) and what
the holdout delivered, across the 19 tuned family champions.

  all families:        rho = 0.414, permutation p = 0.078   <- no evidence of transfer
  better half only:    rho = -0.400, permutation p = 0.289   <- no evidence of transfer

  Read the second line, not the first. A search that only knows which ideas
  are hopeless will score well on the first line while being useless for the
  decision anybody actually makes, which is choosing among the good ones.

  On the holdout, the coin-flip control ranked 1 of 20 family champions.
  Nothing in this pool generalized meaningfully better than random
  entries. Whatever the top of the train column says, that is the
  result.

===== Control survival, selection phase only =====
(during the tuning phase every family keeps its best few by construction,
 so control survival there says nothing.)
  No control candidate ever cleared the survival threshold. That is the
  result you want: the threshold is not passable by luck here.

Saved full results to 'tournament_results/crossdomain_f70.json'

Read this the way the rest of the repo asks you to: the train column was
maximized over and means nothing on its own. Only the holdout columns are
evidence, they were produced by 4465 distinct candidates competing for them,
and the finalists were still chosen by train fitness - so even the holdout figures
carry the selection of 12 survivors out of that pool.
